          "continents": [
            "Australia"
          ],
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "Catostylus mosaicus, also known as the jelly blubber or blue blubber jellyfish, is a species of root-mouth jellyfish of the order root-mouth jellyfish. The jelly blubber is distinguishable by its colour, which ranges from light blue to a dark blue or purple, and its large, rounded bell which pulses in a staccato rhythm. It occurs along the coastline of Eastern Australia in estuaries and shallow bays, and often blooms to high abundance.",
